* text=auto

# why: the git hooks under .githooks/ are executed by /bin/sh, which chokes on
# CRLF line terminators — `* text=auto` above would otherwise check them out
# with CRLF on a Windows clone and silently break the hook (heredocs and `read`
# mangle, so the script no-ops or misfires). Force LF so the hooks — and any
# other shell script — run identically on every platform.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# why (D-24242): the number-allocation ledger is append-only. `merge=union` makes
# git keep BOTH sides' distinct reservation lines on a local rebase/merge, so two
# sessions reserving different WP/EC/D numbers never conflict here (unlike the
# prose-heavy WORK_INDEX / EC_INDEX / DECISIONS). A same-number race is caught
# loudly by `pnpm ledger:numbers:check` (scripts/check-number-ledger.mjs).
docs/ai/NUMBER-LEDGER.md merge=union
